L001091	\subsection{Connection to piezomagnetic coefficients}
L001092	\label{sec:PZM}
L001093	
L001094	
L001095	
L001096	
L001097	
L001098	
L001099	
L001100	
L001101	
L001102	
L001103	In Ref.\,\cite{Bar88}, the PZM coefficient of MnF$_2$ was reported as the magnetization induced by stress, $\sigma_{jk}$:
L001104	
L001105	\begin{equation}
L001106	    M_i=\Lambda_{ijk}\sigma_{jk}.
L001107	    \label{eq:PZM2}
L001108	\end{equation}
L001109	
L001110	The stress $\sigma_{110}$ can be connected to the strain $\varepsilon_{xy}$ using the appropriate Young's modulus $C_0$ and the Poisson ratios via $\sigma_{110}\,=\, \frac{2 C_0}{1+\nu}\varepsilon_{xy}$. Together with the definition of the PZM in the main text, this allows us to express $\lambda$ in terms of the measured $\Lambda$:
L001111	
L001112	\begin{equation}
L001113	\lambda\,\approx\,\frac{\Lambda}{\mu_B \Phi} \frac{2 C_0}{1+\nu}.
L001114	    \label{eq:comparison}
L001115	\end{equation}
L001116	
